    {
      "id": "adjustments-cannot-come-to-more-than-the-order-was-charged",
      "why": "rule 4, #350: an order's adjustments together never exceed its lines in the order's own currency plus its shipping, so what was paid is never negative. The yen line counts for nothing against a deduction in dollars: the ceiling here is the 400 dollar line plus 500 shipping. 901 is refused and stores nothing; 900 is stored",
