      "id": "an-edit-that-leaves-stored-adjustments-too-large-is-refused",
      "why": "rule 4, #350: the ceiling is a rule about the order as it will be stored, not about adjustments. A cheaper line breaks it without mentioning them, and so does a changed order currency, which re-denominates them. The same cheaper line is accepted once the adjustments are lowered in the same edit, and an edit that does not state adjustments leaves them as they are",
